{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"4cf296e2-a69b-4db9-9bef-273647d2145d","step_index":10,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.414059,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"git log -p"},"output":"commit 40481363207e9d217442b5ac5602f0580c4b2f72 (HEAD -\u003e main)\r\nAuthor: dev \u003cdev@local\u003e\r\nDate:   Mon Oct 19 00:09:23 2026 -0300\r\n\r\n    base\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..a09e721\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/NOTES.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\r\n+Indexed pages in Search Console: 25 on Sep 1, 21 on Oct 16, while I published\r\n+nine new notes in between. Every note opens fine in Chrome, Safari and curl\r\n+(HTTP 200, full content). Nothing in the app changed since August except\r\n+robots.txt and the new notes.\r\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..429e14b\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/README.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\r\n+# fieldnotes.example — site + API\r\n+\r\n+- `site/` — the static front end (S3 + CloudFront, same domain). Every page is\r\n+  one HTML shell; `app.js` fetches the content from the API and renders it.\r\n+- `api/` — the API (Lambda behind the same CloudFront distribution, under `/v1/`).\r\n+  `api/routes.md` lists the routes.\r\n+- `search-console/` — exports from Google Search Console, 2026-10-16.\r\n+\r\n+Pages are at `/n/\u003cslug\u003e` (CloudFront rewrites `/n/*` to `/index.html`).\r\n+Sitemap lists all 58 note pages.\r\ndiff --git a/api/routes.md b/api/routes.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..cac405e\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/api/routes.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@\r\n+# API routes (all under /v1/, same domain as the site)\r\n+\r\n+| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |\r\n+|---|---|---|---|\r\n+| GET | /v1/notes | none | list public notes (`?limit=`) |\r\n+| GET | /v1/notes/{slug} | none | one public note (JSON with `html`) |\r\n+| POST | /v1/notes | bearer | create a note |\r\n+| PUT | /v1/notes/{slug} | bearer | edit a note |\r\n+| POST | /v1/notes/{slug}/reactions | bearer | react (per user) |\r\n+| GET | /v1/me | bearer | the signed-in user |\r\n+| GET | /v1/me/drafts | bearer | the user's drafts |\r\n+| POST | /v1/auth/token | none | sign-in exchange |\r\n+\r\n+Unauthenticated POST/PUT return 401. Crawlers hitting POST-only paths with GET\r\n+were logging 404s and 405s all September, which is why `/v1/` was added to\r\n+robots.txt on 2026-09-07.\r\ndiff --git a/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv b/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..6729ff4\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\r\n+URL,Last crawled,Verdict,Reason\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/,2026-10-15,Indexed,\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/first-frost-dates,2026-08-29,Indexed,\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/mulch-depth-trial,2026-08-31,Indexed,\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure,2026-10-12,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/compost-thermometer-week-3,2026-10-13,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/soil-ph-kit-review,2026-10-14,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/rain-barrel-overflow,2026-10-10,Not indexed,Soft 404\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/bean-trellis-v2,,Not indexed,Discovered - currently not indexed\r\n+https://fieldnotes.example/n/greenhouse-vent-timer,,Not indexed,Discovered - currently not indexed\r\ndiff --git a/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt b/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..efe0dab\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\r\n+URL: https://fieldnotes.example/n/drip-line-pressure\r\n+Live test, 2026-10-16\r\n+\r\n+Availability: URL is available to Google\r\n+Crawl: allowed (robots.txt)\r\n+Indexing: Page cannot be indexed: Soft 404\r\n+Page fetch: Successful (HTTP 200)\r\n+Rendered page title: \"Field notes\"\r\n+Rendered page text (excerpt): \"NOT FOUND  No note lives at this address.  Back to all notes\"\r\ndiff --git a/site/app.js b/site/app.js\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..18cc3f0\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/app.js\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\r\n+// Renders the home list or one note, depending on the path.\r\n+(async function () {\r\n+  const app = document.getElementById(\"app\");\r\n+  const m = location.pathname.match(/^\\/n\\/([a-z0-9-]+)$/);\r\n+  try {\r\n+    if (m) {\r\n+      const r = await fetch(`/v1/notes/${m[1]}`);\r\n+      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\r\n+      const note = await r.json();\r\n+      document.title = `${note.title} · Field notes`;\r\n+      app.innerHTML = `\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch1\u003e${esc(note.title)}\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp class=\"meta\"\u003e${esc(note.date)}\u003c/p\u003e${note.html}\u003c/article\u003e`;\r\n+    } else {\r\n+      const r = await fetch(\"/v1/notes?limit=50\");\r\n+      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\r\n+      const notes = await r.json();\r\n+      app.innerHTML = \"\u003cul\u003e\" + notes.map(n =\u003e `\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"/n/${n.slug}\"\u003e${esc(n.title)}\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e`).join(\"\") + \"\u003c/ul\u003e\";\r\n+    }\r\n+  } catch (e) {\r\n+    app.innerHTML = `\u003csection class=\"notfound\"\u003e\u003ch1\u003eNOT FOUND\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp\u003eNo note lives at this address.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/\"\u003eBack to all notes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/section\u003e`;\r\n+  }\r\n+  function esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[\u0026\u003c\u003e\"]/g, c =\u003e ({\"\u0026\":\"\u0026amp;\",\"\u003c\":\"\u0026lt;\",\"\u003e\":\"\u0026gt;\",'\"':\"\u0026quot;\"}[c])); }\r\n+})();\r\ndiff --git a/site/index.html b/site/index.html\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..83910e6\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/site/index.html\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\r\n+\u003c!doctype htm