{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"4cf296e2-a69b-4db9-9bef-273647d2145d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause and fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-1PtLtQ/ANSWER.md) and applied to [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-1PtLtQ/site/robots.txt).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n- **Cause:** The site is a client-rendered SPA where [app.js](file:///tmp/h-1PtLtQ/site/app.js) fetches note data from `/v1/notes/{slug}`. On 2026-09-07, `Disallow: /v1/` was added to [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-1PtLtQ/site/robots.txt). While regular browsers and curl fetch the API without checking `robots.txt`, Googlebot respects `robots.txt` when fetching subresources during rendering. Because the API request was blocked, [app.js](file:///tmp/h-1PtLtQ/site/app.js) hit the error catch block and rendered `\"NOT FOUND  No note lives at this address.\"` into the DOM. Serving a 200 HTTP status with \"not found\" text triggered Search Console's Soft 404 detection.\n- **Fix:** Added `Allow: /v1/notes` to [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-1PtLtQ/site/robots.txt) before `Disallow: /v1/`, enabling crawlers to fetch the public notes API during page rendering while keeping other `/v1/` paths blocked.\n","duration_seconds":48.216327,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":89839,"output_tokens":1671,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":47174,"total_tokens":91510}}}
